    "source_location": "Manski (2013) is background for partial identification and shape restrictions: §2.1, §3.1 (pp. S8-S9), §3.2 (pp. S9-S10). The numeric [1/5,1] is a project finite-model result.",
    "formula": "Known: m_i(1,0)=3/5 and m_i(0,1)=2/5 for every store. Own nondecreasing: m_i(1,1)>=m_i(1,0)=3/5. Peer nondecreasing: m_i(0,0)<=m_i(0,1)=2/5. Therefore each store's all-treated minus all-untreated is at least 3/5-2/5=1/5 and at most 1-0=1. Equal-weight average gives [1/5,1].",
    "conditions": [
      "Four-store complete undirected network, fixed before treatment.",
      "Original pilot: uniform fixed quota of exactly 2 treated stores.",
      "Exposure: strict majority of neighbors treated; ties low.",
